<item><title>Djibouti condemns attacks that damaged Riyadh&apos;s King Abdullah Financial District</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/dj/djibouti-condemns-attacks-that-damaged-riyadh-s-king-5b9d3f/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/dj/djibouti-condemns-attacks-that-damaged-riyadh-s-king-5b9d3f/</guid><category>Djibouti</category><description>The government in Djibouti called the strikes on civilian and economic sites in Saudi Arabia&apos;s capital a flagrant breach of international and humanitarian law.</description><pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 17:03:00 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/dj.jpg" length="31696" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/dj.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Shipping lines&apos; route changes lift Djibouti&apos;s port sector</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/dj/shipping-lines-route-changes-lift-djibouti-s-port-sector-662821/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/dj/shipping-lines-route-changes-lift-djibouti-s-port-sector-662821/</guid><category>Djibouti</category><description>Carriers facing costly detours are beginning to return to the Suez route, a shift Jeune Afrique says favours Djibouti&apos;s container terminal at Doraleh.</description><pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 08:29:56 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/dj/shipping-lines-route-changes-lift-djibouti-s-port-sector-662821/share.jpg" length="41504" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/dj/shipping-lines-route-changes-lift-djibouti-s-port-sector-662821/share.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
